### Thread 1 — `js/postPRReviewComments.js`

**ai-teammate** (2026-10-17):
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: Submodule-remap 422 fallback drops the location prefix (behaviour drift)**

Before the split, `commentText` was mutated in place: when the target was remapped into a submodule, it gained the

```
📍 **`inner/path:line`** (submodule content line)\n\n
```

prefix *before* `scm.addInlineComment(...)` was called. The old `catch` therefore posted the fallback with the prefixed text. In the new structure the plan carries the prefix in `plan.commentText`, but this catch passes the original, unprefixed `commentText`:

```javascript
} catch (error) {
    return fallbackInlineComment(scm, pullRequestId, filePath, inlineComment.line, commentText, error);
}
```

So for a submodule-mapped inline comment whose `addInlineComment` throws (e.g. GitHub 422), the general-PR fallback now reads `📍 **inner/path:line**\n\n<text>` instead of `📍 **inner/path:line**\n\n📍 **inner/path:line** (submodule content line)\n\n<text>`. The reader loses the "(submodule content line)" marker that tells them the location refers to content inside the submodule.

This breaks the ticket's "identical comments on recorded fixtures" guarantee for this (rare) path, and no test pins it. Suggested fix — catch one level deeper so the planned text is in scope:

```javascript
function postAnchoredInlineComment(...) {
    var plan = planInlineAnchor(...);
    ...
    try {
        scm.addInlineComment(pullRequestId, plan.effectivePath, plan.effectiveLine, plan.commentText, plan.startLine, plan.requestedSide);
    } catch (error) {
        return fallbackInlineComment(scm, pullRequestId, filePath, inlineComment.line, plan.commentText, error);
    }
    ...
}
```

`postFallbackInlineComment` still adds its own `📍` line — same as before — so only the inner marker needs the plan's text.

