{"content":"Fixed — the 422 fallback now uses the planned text, restoring the pre-split behavior.

`postAnchoredInlineComment` no longer calls `scm.addInlineComment` directly; the call moved into a new `postPlannedInlineComment` step whose `catch` falls back with `plan.commentText` (which carries the `📍 **inner/path:line** (submodule content line)` prefix) instead of the caller's unprefixed `commentText`:

```javascript
function postPlannedInlineComment(scm, pullRequestId, inlineComment, filePath, plan) {
    try {
        scm.addInlineComment(pullRequestId, plan.effectivePath, plan.effectiveLine, plan.commentText, plan.startLine, plan.requestedSide);
    } catch (error) {
        return fallbackInlineComment(scm, pullRequestId, filePath, inlineComment.line, plan.commentText, error);
    }
    ...
}
```

Regression test added: `gh-949 rework: 422 on a submodule-mapped inline comment falls back with the submodule-content prefix` — a throwing `addInlineComment` on a submodule-mapped target asserts the fallback `addComment` body keeps both the original `📍 **path:line**` line and the `(submodule content line)` marker. It fails on the old code (verified RED) and passes now. `postInlineComment`'s outer catch still guards everything before the plan stage, unchanged.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_1.md"}

{"content":"Done — merged into a single `addPRLabelQuietly(scm, prNumber, label, okMessage, warnPrefix)` with an optional success log:

```javascript
function addPRLabelQuietly(scm, prNumber, label, okMessage, warnPrefix) {
    try {
        scm.addLabel(prNumber, label);
        if (okMessage) console.log(okMessage);
    } catch (labelErr) {
        console.warn(warnPrefix, labelErr.message || labelErr);
    }
}
```

The warn shape is unified to `labelErr.message || labelErr` (the more informative of the two variants), and the two `addPRLabelQuietlyDetailed` call sites (`finishPRAnchoredReview`, `addReviewMarkers`) now pass `okMessage = null`. No log lines changed for the success paths that had them; the ai_pr_reviewed paths stay silent on success as before.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_2.md"}

{"content":"Fixed by hoisting the body resolution back above the `try` — the pre-split failure semantics are restored: a `resolveCommentFileReference`/`readMarkdownFile` failure now propagates to `action()`'s outer catch and posts the loud `❌ PR Review Error` ticket comment instead of being swallowed by the formal-review warn-and-continue.

```javascript
var reviewBody = isApproved
    ? formalApproveBody(generalComment, ticketKey, workingDir)
    : formalRejectBody(generalComment, recommendation, ticketKey, workingDir);
try {
    if (isApproved) {
        applyFormalApprove(scm, pullRequestId, reviewBody);
        return;
    }
    scm.submitReview(pullRequestId, 'REQUEST_CHANGES', reviewBody);
    ...
```

Only the SCM side effects (`dismissReview`/`submitReview`) remain inside the `try`, which is where the deliberate tolerance for provider rejections (e.g. GitHub refusing self-approval) belongs. A comment in `applyFormalGithubReview` records why the boundary sits where it does.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_3.md"}

