`postAnchoredInlineComment` no longer calls `scm.addInlineComment` directly; the call moved into a new `postPlannedInlineComment` step whose `catch` falls back with `plan.commentText` (which carries the `📍 **inner/path:line** (submodule content line)` prefix) instead of the caller's unprefixed `commentText`:

```javascript
function postPlannedInlineComment(scm, pullRequestId, inlineComment, filePath, plan) {
    try {
        scm.addInlineComment(pullRequestId, plan.effectivePath, plan.effectiveLine, plan.commentText, plan.startLine, plan.requestedSide);
    } catch (error) {
        return fallbackInlineComment(scm, pullRequestId, filePath, inlineComment.line, plan.commentText, error);
    }
    ...
}
```

